From: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 23:15:00 +0100
Subject: PCI: quirks: Disable ASPM on the RK3528 root port

ASPM setup sets the Common Clock Configuration bit and retrains the link.
On the RK3528 root port this retrain takes the link down and resets the
endpoint, so it loses its BAR assignments. Seen with an RX 550 on the
ROCK 2F FPC port.

Treat L0s and L1 as unsupported on this root port. ASPM setup then skips
the retrain. "pcie_aspm=off" gives the same result.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz Sobala <lsobala1@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -2552,6 +2552,12 @@
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_HUAWEI, 0x1105, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
 
 /*
+ * RK3528 root port: the common clock retrain done by ASPM setup takes the
+ * link down and resets the endpoint. Without ASPM support there is no retrain.
+ */
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ROCKCHIP, 0x3528, quirk_disable_aspm_l0s_l1);
+
+/*
  * Some Pericom PCIe-to-PCI bridges in reverse mode need the PCIe Retrain
  * Link bit cleared after starting the link retrain process to allow this
  * process to finish.
